invariant: INV-74
file: src/tcp_seal.c
catches: tcp_nonblocking_loop_test
reason: ch_seal_in_place takes a write whose records the key's sequence
  numbers cannot hold before the wrap, so the seal of the record at
  UINT64_MAX refuses after the records before it were sealed, which breaks
  all or nothing, and RFC 9846 §5.3 forbids the wrap. The loop seals three
  records two numbers before the wrap and requires internal_error.

--- old
        if ((uint64_t)count > UINT64_MAX - t->wr.seq) {
--- new
        if (0) {
